Z||000004||SLAMMED87GT||12-03-2001||10:38 PM||||WhiteFiero- I also have those stands on my '87 GT. I got them cheap from some other guy that didn't want them. They needed  finishing work! I simply drilled the bottom to fit in the right place, painted them, and installed. I will be taking them off filling a good part of the bottom of the stands to make them stronger. There is mounting "plates" in the bottom but are thin and not really that great. That is where you need to drill mounting holes. With a little work they look good and put the tail high!!! <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig2_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto540 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||1
Z||000005||WhiteFieroBlur||12-03-2001||11:11 PM||||well these came with no mounting hardware what so ever. So how do I install them? It looks impossible. The bottoms are larger than stock so the stock rubber wouldn't work. i can drill the holes to possibly mount on the wing but I dunno how to make it mount to the decklid. the bottom is tottaly flat and has no opening. Its pitted alot all over. So whats my next step? call these people and say why are there no hardware to install? ||||reg||1
