Z||000007||mrfixit58||12-04-2001||08:08 AM||||Without seeing them, here are my suggeestions: You may consider using something like a collapsible nut system. Something similar to a dry-wall anchor. I was looking in the "Help" section at the local auto parts store noticed some that were for 1/4 inch bolts. All you need to do is line the stands up on the deck lid, mark them, drill the holes and insert the nuts and tighten them down. When you back the bolt out the nut will stay.<P>If you want to use a gasket under the stands like original, you can use an old inner tube. Just trace and cut. IF you want a cleaner install, you can use black RTV and just wipe clean the area around the stands and let it dry. Unfortunately, using the RTV method means that the installation is fairly permanent.<P>Hope this helps,<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P><B>JUST ADDED: </B>1988 GT w/ T-Tops, 5-Speed, and Performance Sound.||||reg||6
